### Parser Recovery — Branch Sync

Use structured `till()` recovery:

```ts
parser.till({
    expected,
    syncTokens,
    title,
    production,
    separator
});
```

Additionally, branches can pass **branch-sync/end-token sets downward** into productions. If a child encounters such a token, it can **yield without consuming it**, allowing the branch parser to recognize and resume at the next sibling/top-level construct.

This lets malformed constructs recover across missing delimiters without swallowing subsequent valid code.
